{"id":"mahabharata-6-055","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":55,"title":"पञ्चपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 55 · Krishna takes up the wheel","summary":{"en":"Bhishma's fury overwhelms the Pandava army, and Arjuna fights only half-heartedly out of reverence for the grandsire. Krishna, to protect his friend, leaps down with a chariot wheel to kill Bhishma, and Arjuna holds him back.","kn":"ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ಕೋಪ ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಮುಳುಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ; ಪಿತಾಮಹನ ಮೇಲಿನ ಗೌರವದಿಂದ ಅರ್ಜುನ ಅರೆಮನಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸ್ನೇಹಿತನನ್ನು ಕಾಯಲು ಕೃಷ್ಣನು ರಥಚಕ್ರ ಹಿಡಿದು ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲಲು ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ಅವನನ್ನು ತಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म का क्रोध पाण्डव सेना को दबा देता है, और अर्जुन पितामह के सम्मान से अनमने ढंग से लड़ते हैं। मित्र की रक्षा के लिए कृष्ण रथ का पहिया लेकर भीष्म को मारने कूद पड़ते हैं, और अर्जुन उन्हें रोक लेते हैं।","te":"భీష్ముని కోపం పాండవసేనను ముంచెత్తుతుంది; పితామహునిపై గౌరవంతో అర్జునుడు అరమనసుతో పోరాడతాడు. స్నేహితుని కాపాడటానికి కృష్ణుడు రథచక్రం పట్టుకుని భీష్ముని చంపడానికి దూకుతాడు; అర్జునుడు అతన్ని ఆపుతాడు.","ta":"பீஷ்மரின் சினம் பாண்டவப் படையை அமிழ்த்துகிறது; பிதாமகர் மீதான மதிப்பால் அர்ஜுனன் அரைமனதுடன் போரிடுகிறான். நண்பனைக் காக்க கண்ணன் தேர்ச்சக்கரத்தை எடுத்துப் பீஷ்மரைக் கொல்லப் பாய, அர்ஜுனன் அவரைத் தடுக்கிறான்.","ml":"ഭീഷ്മരുടെ ക്രോധം പാണ്ഡവ സേനയെ മൂടുന്നു; മുത്തച്ഛനോടുള്ള ബഹുമാനംമൂലം അർജുനൻ പകുതി മനസ്സോടെ മാത്രം പോരാടുന്നു. സുഹൃത്തിനെ രക്ഷിക്കാൻ കൃഷ്ണൻ രഥച്ചക്രവുമായി ഭീഷ്മരെ കൊല്ലാൻ ചാടിയിറങ്ങുന്നു; അർജുനൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ തടയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.55; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रतिज्ञाते तु भीष्मेण तस्मिन्युद्धे सुदारुणे ।\nक्रोधितो मम पुत्रेण दुःखितेन विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Bhishma had made his vow in that dreadful war, and my son, grieved, had angered him especially, what did Bhishma do there, Sanjaya, to the Pandavas?"}},{"n":2,"text":"भीष्मः किमकरोत्तत्र पाण्डवेयेषु संजय ।\nपितामहे वा पाञ्चालास्तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or what did the Panchalas do against the grandsire? Tell me that, Sanjaya."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"गतपूर्वाह्णभूयिष्ठे तस्मिन्नहनि भारत ।\nजयं प्राप्तेषु हृष्टेषु पाण्डवेषु महात्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Most of that day was gone, Bharata, and the great-souled Pandavas, elated, had gained the upper hand."}},{"n":4,"text":"सर्वधर्मविशेषज्ञः पिता देवव्रतस्तव ।\nअभ्ययाज्जवनैरश्वैः पाण्डवानामनीकिनीम् ।\nमहत्या सेनया गुप्तस्तव पुत्रैश्च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father Devavrata, who knew every point of dharma, drove with swift horses against the Pandava host, guarded by a great army and by your sons on every side."}},{"n":5,"text":"प्रावर्तत ततो युद्धं तुमुलं लोमहर्षणम् ।\nअस्माकं पाण्डवैः सार्धमनयात्तव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a tumultuous, hair-raising battle began between our men and the Pandavas, brought on, Bharata, by your own misjudgment."}},{"n":6,"text":"धनुषां कूजतां तत्र तलानां चाभिहन्यताम् ।\nमहान्समभवच्छब्दो गिरीणामिव दीर्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The twang of bows and the slapping of palms against bowguards made a great noise, like mountains being split apart."}},{"n":7,"text":"तिष्ठ स्थितोऽस्मि विद्ध्येनं निवर्तस्व स्थिरो भव ।\nस्थितोऽस्मि प्रहरस्वेति शब्दाः श्रूयन्त सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cries rang out everywhere: \"Stand! I am standing! Strike him! Turn back, be firm! I stand, so strike!\""}},{"n":8,"text":"काञ्चनेषु तनुत्रेषु किरीटेषु ध्वजेषु च ।\nशिलानामिव शैलेषु पतितानामभूत्स्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"On golden armor, crowns and banners there was a sound like boulders falling upon mountains."}},{"n":9,"text":"पतितान्युत्तमाङ्गानि बाहवश्च विभूषिताः ।\nव्यचेष्टन्त महीं प्राप्य शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fallen heads and ornamented arms, lying on the ground, writhed by the hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":10,"text":"हृतोत्तमाङ्गाः केचित्तु तथैवोद्यतकार्मुकाः ।\nप्रगृहीतायुधाश्चापि तस्थुः पुरुषसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some warriors, though their heads were cut off, still stood with bows raised and weapons gripped, the best of men."}},{"n":11,"text":"प्रावर्तत महावेगा नदी रुधिरवाहिनी ।\nमातङ्गाङ्गशिलारौद्रा मांसशोणितकर्दमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A fierce, swift river of blood began to flow, its rocks the bodies of elephants and its mud flesh and gore."}},{"n":12,"text":"वराश्वनरनागानां शरीरप्रभवा तदा ।\nपरलोकार्णवमुखी गृध्रगोमायुमोदिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"It rose from the bodies of fine horses, men and elephants, its mouth opening on the ocean of the other world, a delight to vultures and jackals."}},{"n":13,"text":"न दृष्टं न श्रुतं चापि युद्धमेतादृशं नृप ।\nयथा तव सुतानां च पाण्डवानां च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such a battle was never seen or heard of, king, as this one between your sons and the Pandavas."}},{"n":14,"text":"नासीद्रथपथस्तत्र योधैर्युधि निपातितैः ।\nगजैश्च पतितैर्नीलैर्गिरिशृङ्गैरिवावृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was no room for chariots to pass, for the field was covered with slain warriors and with dark fallen elephants like mountain peaks."}},{"n":15,"text":"विकीर्णैः कवचैश्चित्रैर्ध्वजैश्छत्रैश्च मारिष ।\nशुशुभे तद्रणस्थानं शरदीव नभस्तलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Strewn with bright armor, banners and parasols, that battlefield shone like the autumn sky."}},{"n":16,"text":"विनिर्भिन्नाः शरैः केचिदन्तपीडाविकर्षिणः ।\nअभीताः समरे शत्रूनभ्यधावन्त दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some, pierced by arrows and dragging their entrails, charged fearlessly at their enemies in full armor."}},{"n":17,"text":"तात भ्रातः सखे बन्धो वयस्य मम मातुल ।\nमा मां परित्यजेत्यन्ये चुक्रुशुः पतिता रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others who had fallen cried out, \"Father! Brother! Friend! Kinsman! Comrade! My maternal uncle! Do not leave me!\""}},{"n":18,"text":"आधावाभ्येहि मा गच्छ किं भीतोऽसि क्व यास्यसि ।\nस्थितोऽहं समरे मा भैरिति चान्ये विचुक्रुशुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others shouted, \"Run here, come on, do not go! Why are you afraid, where will you flee? I stand here in battle, do not fear!\""}},{"n":19,"text":"तत्र भीष्मः शांतनवो नित्यं मण्डलकार्मुकः ।\nमुमोच बाणान्दीप्ताग्रानहीनाशीविषानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Bhishma, son of Shantanu, always drawing his bow into a circle, loosed blazing arrows like venomous serpents."}},{"n":20,"text":"शरैरेकायनीकुर्वन्दिशः सर्वा यतव्रतः ।\nजघान पाण्डवरथानादिश्यादिश्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of firm vows, he filled all the directions with arrows into one road and struck down Pandava chariots, one after another, wherever he pointed."}},{"n":21,"text":"स नृत्यन्वै रथोपस्थे दर्शयन्पाणिलाघवम् ।\nअलातचक्रवद्राजंस्तत्र तत्र स्म दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dancing on his chariot-seat and showing the quickness of his hands, he was seen here and there like a whirling firebrand."}},{"n":22,"text":"तमेकं समरे शूरं पाण्डवाः सृञ्जयास्तथा ।\nअनेकशतसाहस्रं समपश्यन्त लाघवात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In battle the Pandavas and Srinjayas saw that single hero, through his speed, as if he were many hundreds of thousands."}},{"n":23,"text":"मायाकृतात्मानमिव भीष्मं तत्र स्म मेनिरे ।\nपूर्वस्यां दिशि तं दृष्ट्वा प्रतीच्यां ददृशुर्जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They thought Bhishma a phantom of illusion: people who saw him in the east saw him in the west as well."}},{"n":24,"text":"उदीच्यां चैनमालोक्य दक्षिणस्यां पुनः प्रभो ।\nएवं स समरे वीरो गाङ्गेयः प्रत्यदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having seen him in the north, lord, they saw him again in the south. So the Ganga's son appeared in battle."}},{"n":25,"text":"न चैनं पाण्डवेयानां कश्चिच्छक्नोति वीक्षितुम् ।\nविशिखानेव पश्यन्ति भीष्मचापच्युतान्बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"None of the Pandava warriors could even look at him; they saw only the many arrows loosed from Bhishma's bow."}},{"n":26,"text":"कुर्वाणं समरे कर्म सूदयानं च वाहिनीम् ।\nव्याक्रोशन्त रणे तत्र वीरा बहुविधं बहु ।\nअमानुषेण रूपेण चरन्तं पितरं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As your father went about in a superhuman form, doing his work in battle and slaughtering their host, the heroes cried out in many ways."}},{"n":27,"text":"शलभा इव राजानः पतन्ति विधिचोदिताः ।\nभीष्माग्निमभि संक्रुद्धं विनाशाय सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings, driven by fate, fell by the thousands to their ruin into the fire of angry Bhishma, like moths."}},{"n":28,"text":"न हि मोघः शरः कश्चिदासीद्भीष्मस्य संयुगे ।\nनरनागाश्वकायेषु बहुत्वाल्लघुवेधिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"No arrow of Bhishma's was ever wasted in that battle: being so many, they struck swiftly into the bodies of men, elephants and horses."}},{"n":29,"text":"भिनत्त्येकेन बाणेन सुमुक्तेन पतत्रिणा ।\nगजकङ्कटसंनाहं वज्रेणेवाचलोत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With one well-loosed feathered shaft he split an elephant's armor, as a thunderbolt splits a great mountain."}},{"n":30,"text":"द्वौ त्रीनपि गजारोहान्पिण्डितान्वर्मितानपि ।\nनाराचेन सुतीक्ष्णेन निजघान पिता तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father killed two or three armored elephant-riders, bunched together, with one keen iron arrow."}},{"n":31,"text":"यो यो भीष्मं नरव्याघ्रमभ्येति युधि कश्चन ।\nमुहूर्तदृष्टः स मया पातितो भुवि दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever came against Bhishma, tiger among men, was seen fallen on the earth after I had seen him for only a moment."}},{"n":32,"text":"एवं सा धर्मराजस्य वध्यमाना महाचमूः ।\nभीष्मेणातुलवीर्येण व्यशीर्यत सहस्रधा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus the great army of King Yudhishthira, struck down by the matchless Bhishma, broke into a thousand pieces."}},{"n":33,"text":"प्रकीर्यत महासेना शरवर्षाभितापिता ।\nपश्यतो वासुदेवस्य पार्थस्य च महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great host, scorched by the rain of arrows, scattered while Vasudeva and the great-souled Partha looked on."}},{"n":34,"text":"यतमानापि ते वीरा द्रवमाणान्महारथान् ।\nनाशक्नुवन्वारयितुं भीष्मबाणप्रपीडिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though the heroes tried, they could not stop their fleeing great warriors, who were tormented by Bhishma's arrows."}},{"n":35,"text":"महेन्द्रसमवीर्येण वध्यमाना महाचमूः ।\nअभज्यत महाराज न च द्वौ सह धावतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down by one whose strength matched Mahendra's, the great army broke, great king, and not even two ran together."}},{"n":36,"text":"आविद्धनरनागाश्वं पतितध्वजकूबरम् ।\nअनीकं पाण्डुपुत्राणां हाहाभूतमचेतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas' army, with men, elephants and horses thrown into confusion, with banners fallen and chariot-poles broken, was senseless, crying out in dismay."}},{"n":37,"text":"जघानात्र पिता पुत्रं पुत्रश्च पितरं तथा ।\nप्रियं सखायं चाक्रन्दे सखा दैवबलात्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Father killed son and son father there, and in the clamor friend killed friend, driven by fate."}},{"n":38,"text":"विमुच्य कवचानन्ये पाण्डुपुत्रस्य सैनिकाः ।\nप्रकीर्य केशान्धावन्तः प्रत्यदृश्यन्त भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other soldiers of the Pandava, throwing off their armor and letting their hair loose, were seen running, Bharata."}},{"n":39,"text":"तद्गोकुलमिवोद्भ्रान्तमुद्भ्रान्तरथयूथपम् ।\nददृशे पाण्डुपुत्रस्य सैन्यमार्तस्वरं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"That army of the Pandava, with its chariot-leaders bewildered, looked like a herd of cattle scattered in panic, crying out in distress."}},{"n":40,"text":"प्रभज्यमानं तत्सैन्यं दृष्ट्वा देवकिनन्दनः ।\nउवाच पार्थं बीभत्सुं निगृह्य रथमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that army breaking up, Devaki's son checked his splendid chariot and spoke to Partha Bibhatsu."}},{"n":41,"text":"अयं स कालः संप्राप्तः पार्थ यः काङ्क्षितस्त्वया ।\nप्रहरास्मै नरव्याघ्र न चेन्मोहाद्विमुह्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said: Partha, this is the time you longed for. Strike him, tiger among men, unless you fall into delusion from confusion."}},{"n":42,"text":"यत्त्वया कथितं वीर पुरा राज्ञां समागमे ।\nभीष्मद्रोणमुखान्सर्वान्धार्तराष्ट्रस्य सैनिकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hero, what you said before in the assembly of kings, scourge of foes, was this: \"I will kill, with their followers, all Dhritarashtra's soldiers led by Bhishma and Drona.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"सानुबन्धान्हनिष्यामि ये मां योत्स्यन्ति संयुगे ।\nइति तत्कुरु कौन्तेय सत्यं वाक्यमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All who fight me in battle I will kill with their kin.\" Make that word true, son of Kunti, subduer of foes."}},{"n":44,"text":"बीभत्सो पश्य सैन्यं स्वं भज्यमानं समन्ततः ।\nद्रवतश्च महीपालान्सर्वान्यौधिष्ठिरे बले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bibhatsu, look at your own army breaking up on every side, and at all the kings fleeing from Yudhishthira's force."}},{"n":45,"text":"दृष्ट्वा हि समरे भीष्मं व्यात्ताननमिवान्तकम् ।\nभयार्ताः संप्रणश्यन्ति सिंहं क्षुद्रमृगा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"For seeing Bhishma in battle like Death with gaping mouth, they flee in terror as small beasts flee a lion."}},{"n":46,"text":"एवमुक्तः प्रत्युवाच वासुदेवं धनंजयः ।\nचोदयाश्वान्यतो भीष्मो विगाह्यैतद्बलार्णवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to thus, Dhananjaya answered Vasudeva: \"Plunge into this ocean of troops and drive the horses toward Bhishma.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"ततोऽश्वान्रजतप्रख्यांश्चोदयामास माधवः ।\nयतो भीष्मरथो राजन्दुष्प्रेक्ष्यो रश्मिमानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Madhava drove the silver-white horses to where Bhishma's chariot stood, king, as hard to look at as the sun."}},{"n":48,"text":"ततस्तत्पुनरावृत्तं युधिष्ठिरबलं महत् ।\nदृष्ट्वा पार्थं महाबाहुं भीष्मायोद्यन्तमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira's great army rallied, seeing the mighty-armed Partha rising to meet Bhishma in battle."}},{"n":49,"text":"ततो भीष्मः कुरुश्रेष्ठः सिंहवद्विनदन्मुहुः ।\nधनंजयरथं तूर्णं शरवर्षैरवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma, best of the Kurus, roaring again and again like a lion, quickly covered Dhananjaya's chariot with showers of arrows."}},{"n":50,"text":"क्षणेन स रथस्तस्य सहयः सहसारथिः ।\nशरवर्षेण महता संछन्नो न प्रकाशते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In an instant that chariot, with its horses and charioteer, vanished from sight, buried in the great rain of arrows."}},{"n":51,"text":"वासुदेवस्त्वसंभ्रान्तो धैर्यमास्थाय सत्त्ववान् ।\nचोदयामास तानश्वान्वितुन्नान्भीष्मसायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Vasudeva, unshaken, firm and strong, steadied himself and urged on the horses, which were wounded by Bhishma's shafts."}},{"n":52,"text":"ततः पार्थो धनुर्गृह्य दिव्यं जलदनिस्वनम् ।\nपातयामास भीष्मस्य धनुश्छित्त्वा त्रिभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha took up his divine bow, which sounded like a thundercloud, and with three arrows cut Bhishma's bow and brought it down."}},{"n":53,"text":"स च्छिन्नधन्वा कौरव्यः पुनरन्यन्महद्धनुः ।\nनिमेषान्तरमात्रेण सज्यं चक्रे पिता तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father, the Kaurava, with his bow cut, strung another great bow in the blink of an eye."}},{"n":54,"text":"विचकर्ष ततो दोर्भ्यां धनुर्जलदनिस्वनम् ।\nअथास्य तदपि क्रुद्धश्चिच्छेद धनुरर्जुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He drew that thundercloud-voiced bow with both arms; but Arjuna, angry, cut that one too."}},{"n":55,"text":"तस्य तत्पूजयामास लाघवं शंतनोः सुतः ।\nसाधु पार्थ महाबाहो साधु भो पाण्डुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Shantanu praised that quickness of his: \"Well done, Partha, mighty-armed! Well done, son of Pandu!"}},{"n":56,"text":"त्वय्येवैतद्युक्तरूपं महत्कर्म धनंजय ।\nप्रीतोऽस्मि सुदृढं पुत्र कुरु युद्धं मया सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"This great deed befits you alone, Dhananjaya. I am deeply pleased, my son. Fight with me.\""}},{"n":57,"text":"इति पार्थं प्रशस्याथ प्रगृह्यान्यन्महद्धनुः ।\nमुमोच समरे वीरः शरान्पार्थरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"So praising Partha, the hero took up another great bow and loosed arrows at Partha's chariot in the battle."}},{"n":58,"text":"अदर्शयद्वासुदेवो हययाने परं बलम् ।\nमोघान्कुर्वञ्शरांस्तस्य मण्डलान्यचरल्लघु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva showed his great skill in driving the horses, making the arrows miss and wheeling the chariot in swift circles."}},{"n":59,"text":"तथापि भीष्मः सुदृढं वासुदेवधनंजयौ ।\nविव्याध निशितैर्बाणैः सर्वगात्रेषु मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Still Bhishma pierced Vasudeva and Dhananjaya hard with sharp arrows over all their limbs, lord."}},{"n":60,"text":"शुशुभाते नरव्याघ्रौ तौ भीष्मशरविक्षतौ ।\nगोवृषाविव नर्दन्तौ विषाणोल्लिखिताङ्कितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wounded by Bhishma's arrows, those two tigers among men shone like two bulls bellowing, marked by the scratches of horns."}},{"n":61,"text":"पुनश्चापि सुसंक्रुद्धः शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nकृष्णयोर्युधि संरब्धो भीष्मो व्यावारयद्दिशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Again, enraged, Bhishma with arrows of smooth joints blocked all directions around the two Krishnas in the fight."}},{"n":62,"text":"वार्ष्णेयं च शरैस्तीक्ष्णैः कम्पयामास रोषितः ।\nमुहुरभ्युत्स्मयन्भीष्मः प्रहस्य स्वनवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angered, he shook the Vrishni, Krishna, with sharp arrows, laughing loudly again and again."}},{"n":63,"text":"ततः कृष्णस्तु समरे दृष्ट्वा भीष्मपराक्रमम् ।\nसंप्रेक्ष्य च महाबाहुः पार्थस्य मृदुयुद्धताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Krishna, seeing Bhishma's prowess and Partha's gentle fighting, and Bhishma pouring out arrows without pause,"}},{"n":64,"text":"भीष्मं च शरवर्षाणि सृजन्तमनिशं युधि ।\nप्रतपन्तमिवादित्यं मध्यमासाद्य सेनयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"blazing like the sun between the two armies,"}},{"n":65,"text":"वरान्वरान्विनिघ्नन्तं पाण्डुपुत्रस्य सैनिकान् ।\nयुगान्तमिव कुर्वाणं भीष्मं यौधिष्ठिरे बले ॥","meaning":{"en":"cutting down the best of the Pandava's soldiers and making Yudhishthira's force like the end of an age,"}},{"n":66,"text":"अमृष्यमाणो भगवान्केशवः परवीरहा ।\nअचिन्तयदमेयात्मा नास्ति यौधिष्ठिरं बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the blessed Keshava, slayer of enemy heroes, could not bear it. Of immeasurable spirit, he thought: \"Yudhishthira's army is finished."}},{"n":67,"text":"एकाह्ना हि रणे भीष्मो नाशयेद्देवदानवान् ।\nकिमु पाण्डुसुतान्युद्धे सबलान्सपदानुगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In a single day Bhishma could destroy gods and demons in battle, how much more the sons of Pandu with their forces and followers?"}},{"n":68,"text":"द्रवते च महत्सैन्यं पाण्डवस्य महात्मनः ।\nएते च कौरवास्तूर्णं प्रभग्नान्दृश्य सोमकान् ।\nआद्रवन्ति रणे हृष्टा हर्षयन्तः पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great army of the great-souled Pandava is fleeing, and these Kauravas, seeing the Somakas routed, rush forward in joy, cheering the grandsire."}},{"n":69,"text":"सोऽहं भीष्मं निहन्म्यद्य पाण्डवार्थाय दंशितः ।\nभारमेतं विनेष्यामि पाण्डवानां महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So today, armored for the Pandavas' sake, I will kill Bhishma and lift this burden from the great-souled Pandavas."}},{"n":70,"text":"अर्जुनोऽपि शरैस्तीक्ष्णैर्वध्यमानो हि संयुगे ।\nकर्तव्यं नाभिजानाति रणे भीष्मस्य गौरवात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, struck by sharp arrows in battle, does not know what he must do, out of reverence for Bhishma.\""}},{"n":71,"text":"तथा चिन्तयतस्तस्य भूय एव पितामहः ।\nप्रेषयामास संक्रुद्धः शरान्पार्थरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"While he thought thus, the grandsire again, enraged, sent arrows at Partha's chariot."}},{"n":72,"text":"तेषां बहुत्वाद्धि भृशं शराणां\nदिशोऽथ सर्वाः पिहिता बभूवुः ।\nन चान्तरिक्षं न दिशो न भूमि-\nर्न भास्करोऽदृश्यत रश्मिमाली ।\nववुश्च वातास्तुमुलाः सधूमा\nदिशश्च सर्वाः क्षुभिता बभूवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So many were those arrows that all the directions were shut out. Neither sky, nor directions, nor earth, nor the sun with his rays could be seen. Fierce winds blew, full of smoke, and all the quarters were in turmoil."}},{"n":73,"text":"द्रोणो विकर्णोऽथ जयद्रथश्च\nभूरिश्रवाः कृतवर्मा कृपश्च ।\nश्रुतायुरम्बष्ठपतिश्च राजा\nविन्दानुविन्दौ च सुदक्षिणश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, Vikarna, Jayadratha, Bhurishravas, Kritavarma, Kripa, Shrutayu, the king of the Ambashthas, Vinda and Anuvinda, and Sudakshina,"}},{"n":74,"text":"प्राच्याश्च सौवीरगणाश्च सर्वे\nवसातयः क्षुद्रकमालवाश्च ।\nकिरीटिनं त्वरमाणाभिसस्रु-\nर्निदेशगाः शांतनवस्य राज्ञः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Easterners, all the Sauviras, the Vasatis, the Kshudrakas and Malavas, acting on the command of King Bhishma, Shantanu's son, rushed swiftly at Kiritin."}},{"n":75,"text":"तं वाजिपादातरथौघजालै-\nरनेकसाहस्रशतैर्ददर्श ।\nकिरीटिनं संपरिवार्यमाणं\nशिनेर्नप्ता वारणयूथपैश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The grandson of Shini, Satyaki, saw him surrounded by thousands of hundreds of masses of horse, foot, chariots and elephant herds."}},{"n":76,"text":"ततस्तु दृष्ट्वार्जुनवासुदेवौ\nपदातिनागाश्वरथैः समन्तात् ।\nअभिद्रुतौ शस्त्रभृतां वरिष्ठौ\nशिनिप्रवीरोऽभिससार तूर्णम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing Arjuna and Vasudeva attacked on every side by foot, elephants, horses and chariots, the hero of the Shinis, best of the weapon-bearers, rushed swiftly to them."}},{"n":77,"text":"स तान्यनीकानि महाधनुष्मा-\nञ्शिनिप्रवीरः सहसाभिपत्य ।\nचकार साहाय्यमथार्जुनस्य\nविष्णुर्यथा वृत्रनिषूदनस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great archer, hero of the Shinis, suddenly fell on those troops and helped Arjuna, as Vishnu helped the slayer of Vritra."}},{"n":78,"text":"विशीर्णनागाश्वरथध्वजौघं\nभीष्मेण वित्रासितसर्वयोधम् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरानीकमभिद्रवन्तं\nप्रोवाच संदृश्य शिनिप्रवीरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Yudhishthira's army fleeing, with elephants, horses, chariots and banners scattered and all warriors terrified by Bhishma, the Shini hero spoke to them."}},{"n":79,"text":"क्व क्षत्रिया यास्यथ नैष धर्मः\nसतां पुरस्तात्कथितः पुराणैः ।\nमा स्वां प्रतिज्ञां जहत प्रवीराः\nस्वं वीरधर्मं परिपालयध्वम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki said: Where are you going, kshatriyas? This is not the dharma that the ancients taught to good men. Do not abandon your own vow, heroes; keep your warrior's duty."}},{"n":80,"text":"तान्वासवानन्तरजो निशम्य\nनरेन्द्रमुख्यान्द्रवतः समन्तात् ।\nपार्थस्य दृष्ट्वा मृदुयुद्धतां च\nभीष्मं च संख्ये समुदीर्यमाणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, the lord of the Dasharhas, heard those words of Satyaki and saw the best of kings fleeing on all sides, Partha's gentle fighting, and Bhishma roaring in battle."}},{"n":81,"text":"अमृष्यमाणः स ततो महात्मा\nयशस्विनं सर्वदशार्हभर्ता ।\nउवाच शैनेयमभिप्रशंस-\nन्दृष्ट्वा कुरूनापततः समन्तात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unable to bear it, that great-souled one praised the renowned Shaineya as the Kurus came rushing from all sides."}},{"n":82,"text":"ये यान्ति यान्त्वेव शिनिप्रवीर\nयेऽपि स्थिताः सात्वत तेऽपि यान्तु ।\nभीष्मं रथात्पश्य निपात्यमानं\nद्रोणं च संख्ये सगणं मयाद्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said: Let those who go, go, hero of the Shinis; let those who stay, Satvata, go also. Watch me today throw Bhishma from his chariot, and Drona with his followers."}},{"n":83,"text":"नासौ रथः सात्वत कौरवाणां\nक्रुद्धस्य मुच्येत रणेऽद्य कश्चित् ।\nतस्मादहं गृह्य रथाङ्गमुग्रं\nप्राणं हरिष्यामि महाव्रतस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one of the Kauravas on that chariot will escape me when I am angry. So I will take up my fearsome discus and take the life of him of the great vow."}},{"n":84,"text":"निहत्य भीष्मं सगणं तथाजौ\nद्रोणं च शैनेय रथप्रवीरम् ।\nप्रीतिं करिष्यामि धनंजयस्य\nराज्ञश्च भीमस्य तथाश्विनोश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed Bhishma and his followers in battle, and Drona, the chariot-hero, Shaineya, I will please Dhananjaya, King Yudhishthira, Bhima, and the Ashvins."}},{"n":85,"text":"निहत्य सर्वान्धृतराष्ट्रपुत्रां-\nस्तत्पक्षिणो ये च नरेन्द्रमुख्याः ।\nराज्येन राजानमजातशत्रुं\nसंपादयिष्याम्यहमद्य हृष्टः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed all Dhritarashtra's sons and the kings who side with them, today in joy I will give King Ajatashatru the kingdom."}},{"n":86,"text":"ततः सुनाभं वसुदेवपुत्रः\nसूर्यप्रभं वज्रसमप्रभावम् ।\nक्षुरान्तमुद्यम्य भुजेन चक्रं\nरथादवप्लुत्य विसृज्य वाहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vasudeva's son leapt from his chariot, letting the horses go, and raised in his arm the discus Sudarshana, bright as the sun, as strong as lightning, with a razor's edge."}},{"n":87,"text":"संकम्पयन्गां चरणैर्महात्मा\nवेगेन कृष्णः प्रससार भीष्मम् ।\nमदान्धमाजौ समुदीर्णदर्पः\nसिंहो जिघांसन्निव वारणेन्द्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaking the earth with his feet, the great-souled Krishna swiftly rushed at Bhishma, like a lion mad to kill a rutting elephant, swollen with pride."}},{"n":88,"text":"सोऽभ्यद्रवद्भीष्ममनीकमध्ये\nक्रुद्धो महेन्द्रावरजः प्रमाथी ।\nव्यालम्बिपीतान्तपटश्चकाशे\nघनो यथा खेऽचिरभापिनद्धः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Furious, Indra's younger brother, the crusher, ran at Bhishma in the midst of the army, his hanging yellow garment shining like a cloud with lightning wrapped around it."}},{"n":89,"text":"सुदर्शनं चास्य रराज शौरे-\nस्तच्चक्रपद्मं सुभुजोरुनालम् ।\nयथादिपद्मं तरुणार्कवर्णं\nरराज नारायणनाभिजातम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That discus of Shauri, with its fine arms and thighs for its stalk, shone like a lotus, as the first lotus, tender as the young sun, shone born from Narayana's navel."}},{"n":90,"text":"तत्कृष्णकोपोदयसूर्यबुद्धं\nक्षुरान्ततीक्ष्णाग्रसुजातपत्रम् ।\nतस्यैव देहोरुसरःप्ररूढं\nरराज नारायणबाहुनालम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Awakened by the rising sun of Krishna's anger, with its razor edge as sharp-tipped petals, it shone, grown in the lake of his own body, a lotus on the stalk of Narayana's arm."}},{"n":91,"text":"तमात्तचक्रं प्रणदन्तमुच्चैः\nक्रुद्धं महेन्द्रावरजं समीक्ष्य ।\nसर्वाणि भूतानि भृशं विनेदुः\nक्षयं कुरूणामिति चिन्तयित्वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the furious younger brother of Mahendra, discus in hand, roaring loudly, all beings cried out in terror, thinking of the destruction of the Kurus."}},{"n":92,"text":"स वासुदेवः प्रगृहीतचक्रः\nसंवर्तयिष्यन्निव जीवलोकम् ।\nअभ्युत्पतँल्लोकगुरुर्बभासे\nभूतानि धक्ष्यन्निव कालवह्निः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva, discus raised, as if about to dissolve the world, rose up, the teacher of the worlds, blazing like the fire of time about to burn creatures."}},{"n":93,"text":"तमापतन्तं प्रगृहीतचक्रं\nसमीक्ष्य देवं द्विपदां वरिष्ठम् ।\nअसंभ्रमात्कार्मुकबाणपाणी\nरथे स्थितः शांतनवोऽभ्युवाच ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the god, best of two-legged beings, rushing at him with the discus raised, Shantanu's son, unshaken, bow and arrows in hand, standing on his chariot, said to him:"}},{"n":94,"text":"एह्येहि देवेश जगन्निवास\nनमोऽस्तु ते शार्ङ्गरथाङ्गपाणे ।\nप्रसह्य मां पातय लोकनाथ\nरथोत्तमाद्भूतशरण्य संख्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said: Come, come, lord of the gods, home of the world! Homage to you, bearer of the Sharnga bow and discus! Throw me down forcibly from this best of chariots, refuge of beings, lord of the worlds, in battle."}},{"n":95,"text":"त्वया हतस्येह ममाद्य कृष्ण\nश्रेयः परस्मिन्निह चैव लोके ।\nसंभावितोऽस्म्यन्धकवृष्णिनाथ\nलोकैस्त्रिभिर्वीर तवाभियानात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I am slain by you today, Krishna, there is blessing for me here and in the next world. I am honored, hero, lord of the Andhakas and Vrishnis, by your coming at me in the three worlds."}},{"n":96,"text":"रथादवप्लुत्य ततस्त्वरावा-\nन्पार्थोऽप्यनुद्रुत्य यदुप्रवीरम् ।\nजग्राह पीनोत्तमलम्बबाहुं\nबाह्वोर्हरिं व्यायतपीनबाहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha too leapt in haste from his chariot and ran after the Yadava hero, and with his long, stout arms seized Hari by both his arms."}},{"n":97,"text":"निगृह्यमाणश्च तदादिदेवो\nभृशं सरोषः किल नाम योगी ।\nआदाय वेगेन जगाम विष्णु-\nर्जिष्णुं महावात इवैकवृक्षम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though held, the primeval god, a yogi, raged fiercely, and Vishnu dragged Jishnu along swiftly, as a great wind drags a single tree."}},{"n":98,"text":"पार्थस्तु विष्टभ्य बलेन पादौ\nभीष्मान्तिकं तूर्णमभिद्रवन्तम् ।\nबलान्निजग्राह किरीटमाली\nपदेऽथ राजन्दशमे कथंचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Partha dug in his feet with force and, holding back him who was rushing swiftly toward Bhishma, the crowned one stopped him with difficulty at the tenth step, king."}},{"n":99,"text":"अवस्थितं च प्रणिपत्य कृष्णं\nप्रीतोऽर्जुनः काञ्चनचित्रमाली ।\nउवाच कोपं प्रतिसंहरेति\nगतिर्भवान्केशव पाण्डवानाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, pleased, wearing his golden garland, bowed to Krishna as he stood and said: \"Restrain your anger. You are the refuge of the Pandavas."}},{"n":100,"text":"न हास्यते कर्म यथाप्रतिज्ञं\nपुत्रैः शपे केशव सोदरैश्च ।\nअन्तं करिष्यामि यथा कुरूणां\nत्वयाहमिन्द्रानुज संप्रयुक्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By my sons and brothers, Keshava, I swear: I will not let my deed fall short of my vow. I will make an end of the Kurus, with you as my driver, younger brother of Indra.\""}},{"n":101,"text":"ततः प्रतिज्ञां समयं च तस्मै\nजनार्दनः प्रीतमना निशम्य ।\nस्थितः प्रिये कौरवसत्तमस्य\nरथं सचक्रः पुनरारुरोह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Janardana, hearing his vow and promise, was glad, and, standing to do what pleased the best of the Kurus, he climbed back on his chariot with discus in hand."}},{"n":102,"text":"स तानभीषून्पुनराददानः\nप्रगृह्य शङ्खं द्विषतां निहन्ता ।\nविनादयामास ततो दिशश्च\nस पाञ्चजन्यस्य रवेण शौरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up again the fearless reins and grasping his conch, the slayer of foes made all the directions ring with the sound of the Panchajanya."}},{"n":103,"text":"व्याविद्धनिष्काङ्गदकुण्डलं तं\nरजोविकीर्णाञ्चितपक्ष्मनेत्रम् ।\nविशुद्धदंष्ट्रं प्रगृहीतशङ्खं\nविचुक्रुशुः प्रेक्ष्य कुरुप्रवीराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kuru heroes cried out at the sight of him, his armlets and earrings swinging, his eyes with fine lashes dusted with dirt, his teeth bright, holding the conch."}},{"n":104,"text":"मृदङ्गभेरीपटहप्रणादा\nनेमिस्वना दुन्दुभिनिस्वनाश्च ।\nससिंहनादाश्च बभूवुरुग्राः\nसर्वेष्वनीकेषु ततः कुरूणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then fearsome sounds arose in all the Kuru divisions: of mridangas, bheris, drums, wheel-sounds and dundubhis, with lions' roars."}},{"n":105,"text":"गाण्डीवघोषः स्तनयित्नुकल्पो\nजगाम पार्थस्य नभो दिशश्च ।\nजग्मुश्च बाणा विमलाः प्रसन्नाः\nसर्वा दिशः पाण्डवचापमुक्ताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The thunder-like twang of Gandiva filled the sky and the directions, and bright, clear arrows loosed from the Pandava's bow flew to every quarter."}},{"n":106,"text":"तं कौरवाणामधिपो बलेन\nभीष्मेण भूरिश्रवसा च सार्धम् ।\nअभ्युद्ययावुद्यतबाणपाणिः\nकक्षं दिधक्षन्निव धूमकेतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord of the Kauravas came against him with his troops, with Bhishma and Bhurishravas, arrows raised in hand, like a comet wishing to burn a dry thicket."}},{"n":107,"text":"अथार्जुनाय प्रजहार भल्ला-\nन्भूरिश्रवाः सप्त सुवर्णपुङ्खान् ।\nदुर्योधनस्तोमरमुग्रवेगं\nशल्यो गदां शांतनवश्च शक्तिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhurishravas hurled seven gold-feathered barbed arrows at Arjuna; Duryodhana a javelin of terrible speed; Shalya a mace; and Shantanu's son a spear."}},{"n":108,"text":"स सप्तभिः सप्त शरप्रवेका-\nन्संवार्य भूरिश्रवसा विसृष्टान् ।\nशितेन दुर्योधनबाहुमुक्तं\nक्षुरेण तत्तोमरमुन्ममाथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna checked the seven finest arrows sent by Bhurishravas with seven of his own, and with a sharp razor-headed arrow smashed the javelin loosed by Duryodhana."}},{"n":109,"text":"ततः शुभामापततीं स शक्तिं\nविद्युत्प्रभां शांतनवेन मुक्ताम् ।\nगदां च मद्राधिपबाहुमुक्तां\nद्वाभ्यां शराभ्यां निचकर्त वीरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that hero cut with two arrows the lightning-bright spear flung by Shantanu's son as it came, and the mace thrown by the lord of the Madras."}},{"n":110,"text":"ततो भुजाभ्यां बलवद्विकृष्य\nचित्रं धनुर्गाण्डिवमप्रमेयम् ।\nमाहेन्द्रमस्त्रं विधिवत्सुघोरं\nप्रादुश्चकाराद्भुतमन्तरिक्षे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, drawing the wondrous bow Gandiva, the immeasurable one, forcibly with both arms, he duly called forth in the sky the terrible Mahendra weapon."}},{"n":111,"text":"तेनोत्तमास्त्रेण ततो महात्मा\nसर्वाण्यनीकानि महाधनुष्मान् ।\nशरौघजालैर्विमलाग्निवर्णै-\nर्निवारयामास किरीटमाली ॥","meaning":{"en":"With that supreme weapon the great-souled, great archer, the crowned one, held back all the divisions with webs of arrows bright as clear fire."}},{"n":112,"text":"शिलीमुखाः पार्थधनुःप्रमुक्ता\nरथान्ध्वजाग्राणि धनूंषि बाहून् ।\nनिकृत्य देहान्विविशुः परेषां\nनरेन्द्रनागेन्द्रतुरंगमाणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The arrows loosed from Partha's bow cut chariots, banner-tops, bows and arms, and entered the bodies of enemy kings, great elephants and horses."}},{"n":113,"text":"ततो दिशश्चानुदिशश्च पार्थः\nशरैः सुधारैर्निशितैर्वितत्य ।\nगाण्डीवशब्देन मनांसि तेषां\nकिरीटमाली व्यथयां चकार ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha, spreading them across the directions and intermediate directions with sharp, well-shaped arrows, tormented their minds with the sound of Gandiva."}},{"n":114,"text":"तस्मिंस्तथा घोरतमे प्रवृत्ते\nशङ्खस्वना दुन्दुभिनिस्वनाश्च ।\nअन्तर्हिता गाण्डिवनिस्वनेन\nबभूवुरुग्राश्च रणप्रणादाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that most dreadful fight went on, the sounds of conches and dundubhis were drowned by Gandiva's roar, and the fierce battle-cries were lost."}},{"n":115,"text":"गाण्डीवशब्दं तमथो विदित्वा\nविराटराजप्रमुखा नृवीराः ।\nपाञ्चालराजो द्रुपदश्च वीर-\nस्तं देशमाजग्मुरदीनसत्त्वाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the sound of Gandiva, Virata and the other heroes, and King Drupada of Panchala, of unflinching courage, came to that place."}},{"n":116,"text":"सर्वाणि सैन्यानि तु तावकानि\nयतो यतो गाण्डिवजः प्रणादः ।\nततस्ततः संनतिमेव जग्मु-\nर्न तं प्रतीपोऽभिससार कश्चित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wherever the sound of Gandiva rose, all your armies bowed away from it; no one went against him."}},{"n":117,"text":"तस्मिन्सुघोरे नृपसंप्रहारे\nहताः प्रवीराः सरथाः ससूताः ।\nगजाश्च नाराचनिपाततप्ता\nमहापताकाः शुभरुक्मकक्ष्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that dreadful clash of kings, heroes were killed with their chariots and charioteers, and elephants with great banners and fine gold girths, scorched by the fall of iron arrows."}},{"n":118,"text":"परीतसत्त्वाः सहसा निपेतुः\nकिरीटिना भिन्नतनुत्रकायाः ।\nदृढाहताः पत्रिभिरुग्रवेगैः\nपार्थेन भल्लैर्निशितैः शिताग्रैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their strength gone, they suddenly fell, their armor and bodies torn by the crowned one, struck hard by terrible-speed arrows and sharp, keen-tipped barbed shafts of Partha."}},{"n":119,"text":"निकृत्तयन्त्रा निहतेन्द्रकीला\nध्वजा महान्तो ध्वजिनीमुखेषु ।\nपदातिसंघाश्च रथाश्च संख्ये\nहयाश्च नागाश्च धनंजयेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great banners at the front of the divisions, their machinery cut and their Indra-pegs struck down, fell; so did masses of foot soldiers, chariots, horses and elephants, felled by Dhananjaya."}},{"n":120,"text":"बाणाहतास्तूर्णमपेतसत्त्वा\nविष्टभ्य गात्राणि निपेतुरुर्व्याम् ।\nऐन्द्रेण तेनास्त्रवरेण राज-\nन्महाहवे भिन्नतनुत्रदेहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by arrows, they lost heart at once and fell to the earth with stiff limbs, great king, their armor and bodies broken in the great battle by that supreme weapon of Indra."}},{"n":121,"text":"ततः शरौघैर्निशितैः किरीटिना\nनृदेहशस्त्रक्षतलोहितोदा ।\nनदी सुघोरा नरदेहफेना\nप्रवर्तिता तत्र रणाजिरे वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in the arena of battle the crowned one with sharp showers of arrows made a most dreadful river, whose water was the blood from wounds by weapons in human bodies, and whose foam was human bodies."}},{"n":122,"text":"वेगेन सातीव पृथुप्रवाहा\nप्रसुस्रुता भैरवारावरूपा ।\nपरेतनागाश्वशरीररोधा\nनरान्त्रमज्जाभृतमांसपङ्का ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wide and swift in its flow, it surged with fearful roars, its banks dead elephants and horses, its mud of flesh, human entrails and marrow."}},{"n":123,"text":"प्रभूतरक्षोगणभूतसेविता\nशिरःकपालाकुलकेशशाद्वला ।\nशरीरसंघातसहस्रवाहिनी\nविशीर्णनानाकवचोर्मिसंकुला ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was frequented by hosts of demons and spirits, with skulls and tangled hair for its grass, bearing thousands of heaps of bodies, filled with the waves of scattered armor."}},{"n":124,"text":"नराश्वनागास्थिनिकृत्तशर्करा\nविनाशपातालवती भयावहा ।\nतां कङ्कमालावृतगृध्रकह्वैः\nक्रव्यादसंघैश्च तरक्षुभिश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its pebbles were the bones of men, horses and elephants cut away, a place of destruction like a nether world, terrible. It was bordered with flocks of herons, vultures, kankas, and carrion-eaters and hyenas."}},{"n":125,"text":"उपेतकूलां ददृशुः समन्ता-\nत्क्रूरां महावैतरणीप्रकाशाम् ।\nप्रवर्तितामर्जुनबाणसंघै-\nर्मेदोवसासृक्प्रवहां सुभीमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All around they saw it, cruel, like the great Vaitarani, carrying fat, marrow and blood, brought forth by Arjuna's masses of arrows, most fearful."}},{"n":126,"text":"ते चेदिपाञ्चालकरूषमत्स्याः\nपार्थाश्च सर्वे सहिताः प्रणेदुः ।\nवित्रास्य सेनां ध्वजिनीपतीनां\nसिंहो मृगाणामिव यूथसंघान् ।\nविनेदतुस्तावतिहर्षयुक्तौ\nगाण्डीवधन्वा च जनार्दनश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Chedis, Panchalas, Karushas, Matsyas and all the Parthas together roared, having terrified the commanders' army as a lion terrifies herds of deer. Overjoyed, Gandiva's wielder and Janardana both roared aloud."}},{"n":127,"text":"ततो रविं संहृतरश्मिजालं\nदृष्ट्वा भृशं शस्त्रपरिक्षताङ्गाः ।\nतदैन्द्रमस्त्रं विततं सुघोर-\nमसह्यमुद्वीक्ष्य युगान्तकल्पम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing the sun with his rays withdrawn, and seeing that dreadful, unbearable Indra weapon spread out like the end of an age, the Kurus, wounded by weapons all over,"}},{"n":128,"text":"अथापयानं कुरवः सभीष्माः\nसद्रोणदुर्योधनबाह्लिकाश्च ।\nचक्रुर्निशां संधिगतां समीक्ष्य\nविभावसोर्लोहितराजियुक्ताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"with Bhishma, Drona, Duryodhana and the Bahlikas, withdrew from battle, seeing the evening twilight come, streaked with the red of the sun."}},{"n":129,"text":"अवाप्य कीर्तिं च यशश्च लोके\nविजित्य शत्रूंश्च धनंजयोऽपि ।\nययौ नरेन्द्रैः सह सोदरैश्च\nसमाप्तकर्मा शिबिरं निशायाम् ।\nततः प्रजज्ञे तुमुलः कुरूणां\nनिशामुखे घोरतरः प्रणादः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having won fame and glory in the world and defeated his foes, Dhananjaya, his work done, went with the kings and his brothers to camp at night. Then at nightfall a dreadful, tumultuous roar rose among the Kurus."}},{"n":130,"text":"रणे रथानामयुतं निहत्य\nहता गजाः सप्तशतार्जुनेन ।\nप्राच्याश्च सौवीरगणाश्च सर्वे\nनिपातिताः क्षुद्रकमालवाश्च ।\nमहत्कृतं कर्म धनंजयेन\nकर्तुं यथा नार्हति कश्चिदन्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In the battle Arjuna killed ten thousand chariots, and seven hundred elephants. The Easterners, all the Sauviras, the Kshudrakas and Malavas have been struck down. Dhananjaya did a great deed such as no one else could do."}},{"n":131,"text":"श्रुतायुरम्बष्ठपतिश्च राजा\nतथैव दुर्मर्षणचित्रसेनौ ।\nद्रोणः कृपः सैन्धवबाह्लिकौ च\nभूरिश्रवाः शल्यशलौ च राजन् ।\nस्वबाहुवीर्येण जिताः सभीष्माः\nकिरीटिना लोकमहारथेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"King of the Ambashthas Shrutayu, Durmarshana and Chitrasena, Drona, Kripa, the Sindhu king and Bahlika, Bhurishravas, Shalya and Shala, king, with Bhishma, were all conquered by the strength of the arms of Kiritin, the great chariot-warrior of the world.\""}},{"n":132,"text":"इति ब्रुवन्तः शिबिराणि जग्मुः\nसर्वे गणा भारत ये त्वदीयाः ।\nउल्कासहस्रैश्च सुसंप्रदीप्तै-\nर्विभ्राजमानैश्च तथा प्रदीपैः ।\nकिरीटिवित्रासितसर्वयोधा\nचक्रे निवेशं ध्वजिनी कुरूणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying this, all your troops, Bharata, went to their camps with thousands of blazing torches and brilliant lamps. The Kuru army, with all its warriors terrified by Kiritin, made its camp."}}]}]}